---
deploy.proxy
  Serve sites over HTTPS with Caddy, proxied to their upstreams
  Applies to this host.

Why
  An app published on 127.0.0.1 is safe from the internet but also out of its
  reach. Caddy in front of it serves it over HTTPS, gets and renews the
  certificates by itself, and redirects HTTP to HTTPS.

Params (in the module's profile table)
  sites (default [])
      Required: the sites Caddy serves, e.g. [{ domain = "app.example.com",
      upstream = "127.0.0.1:8080" }]. Each domain needs a DNS record for this
      host and ports 80 and 443 open.

Fixes these audit controls
  none
